# Closest Nyström competitor: source gap narrowed

Primary paper https://arxiv.org/pdf/2502.13570v4, arXiv2026-04-20, title-page2026-04-21. Read Sections4–6, Algorithm4.1, Lemma5.1 and experimental settings. Pooled landmark selection supports permutation equivariance. The paper already describes single-pass aggregation for all permutations with O(P*l) accumulator space plus O(P*n) permutation bits; streaming feature means is not a new contribution. Gaussian correlated-data comparison uses nX=nY=2500,d=3,rho1=.5,rho2=.51–.66,199 permutations,400 power/1000 null repetitions and Wilson intervals. It compares RFF/CTT with uniform/AKRLS Nyström; these are published, not our measured results.

Paper code URL redirects to https://github.com/mletizia/nystrom-mmd-paper . Inspected commit ddb9b2cacc092841518c3d4e18b745f266d8f517; byte/Git blob identities in sources/nystrom_source_manifest_v1.json. No root license located, so source bodies remain reproducible .deps, not newly redistributed. README's standalone-package main ref returned404; paper source remains usable. This is not a project-wide block.

Code facts (not executed): tests.py NysMMDtest forms full n*l features and three float64 (B+1)*n indicator arrays I,I_X,I_Y, unlike the paper's memory-lean presentation. nystrom.py clips all singular values below1e-12 before inverse square-root, rather than an exact Moore-Penrose zeroing rule. nys_inds(uniform) samples pooled indices without replacement. Both it and the outer permutation generator are initialized from the same integer seed; actual dependence/equivariance needs a targeted audit before claiming violation. Merely sharing a seed is not proof of invalid testing.

Correlated experiment script fits bandwidth on an external generated sample and standardizes test data by pooled mean/std; rMMDtest is called with sqrt(2)*sigma and creates cosine+sine features, so its argument R produces2R real features. Do not equate its R directly with goodpoints' random-phase r when matching state. Script default K ends at500 and omits CTT dispatch although saved paper results contain CTT. Determine exact revision/adapter used before claiming full figure reproduction. No source claim above overturns published results.

Next narrow question: can the exact native projected-MMD path and its permutation decision be reproduced on a bounded correlated-Gaussian case with correct bandwidth/feature-count conventions, and which source-versus-paper deviations matter? Before new numerics, freeze a native diagnostic: unequal/equal-count mean weights; repeated/near-coincident landmark handling versus independent pseudoinverse reference; seeds/permutation/landmark dependency; retained full scores and complete costs. Reuse current CTT/Cheap baselines, include native Cheap RFF if proceeding to quality comparisons. Separate a justified implementation correction from a proposed new method. Do not repeat completed CTT normalization/cost work or infer power from3 trials.
